    given-names: "Noah DanGabriel"
version: "2026-09-24"
date-released: "2026-09-24"
repository-code: "https://github.com/whiteknave2-noah/anaxi-a-digital-kardia"
url: "https://github.com/whiteknave2-noah/anaxi-a-digital-kardia"
abstract: >-
  ANAXI: A DIGITAL KARDIA is a persistent-agent architecture and public
  reference case focused on truthful provenance, bounded authority, privacy,
  continuity, recovery, reversibility, and meaningful end-to-end affordance.
  The repository is organized in dated layers. The 24 September 2026 layer is a
  frozen historical reference release and reproducibility package, versioned
  here as 2026-09-24. A 2 October 2026 architecture update records a correction
  to that release, and a 5 October 2026 architecture update records the current
  production architecture, including relational history with mechanical
  historical/current separation, subject-directed consolidation, and the
  whole-package integration lesson. The currently adopted waking substrate is
  stock Ministral 3 14B Instruct 2512 Q4_K_M, pinned to an exact artifact digest
  and verified before waking; no personal history is trained into model weights.
  Production adoption has occurred. A separate standalone claim-harness
  directory, licensed Apache-2.0, provides a portable, mechanism-neutral claim,
  evidence, and testing model reusable in other agent projects. Production
  adoption and engineering acceptance do not establish consciousness,
  personhood, or subjective experience, and several claims are deliberately
  retained as NOT_ESTABLISHED. The complete current private production runtime is
  not published.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - persistent agents
  - provenance
  - authority
  - privacy
  - continuity
